    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\">\n  <strong>A DeepSeek Harness web plugin that shows every session's conversation progress and token usage at a glance.</strong><br>\n  <em>All-windows overview · session analysis · cost estimation · token heatmap.</em><br>\n  <strong>100% read-only and local</strong> — no outbound requests, no session writes.\n</p>\n\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"assets/window-stats.png\" alt=\"Window Stats\" width=\"100%\"></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"assets/session-analytics.png\" alt=\"Session Analysis\" width=\"100%\"></p>\n\n<p align=\"center\"><img src=\"assets/overview.png\" alt=\"Overview panel and sidebar summary\" width=\"100%\"></p>"
    },
    {
      "section": "What this plugin provides",
      "text": "Installing this bundle adds a cross-session observability surface to every session of the target dsh profile. It reads the official `tokenUsage` / `sessionStats` / `contextPressure` / `contextBreakdown` projections (plus a `tokenHistory` projection it registers itself), so no host service or new RPC is required beyond that one projection unit."
    },
    {
      "section": "What this plugin provides",
      "text": "| Surface | What it shows |\n|---|---|\n| `窗口统计` view tab | One row per session: status, turns/steps, input/output tokens, cache-hit ratio, context occupancy, duration, cost, last activity — with sort / filter / group-by-workspace / model & currency selectors, and a right detail panel (token buckets, context composition, timing, heatmap). |\n| `会话分析` view tab | Time-range analysis (presets + custom) of the current session: token trend chart, tool-type duration distribution (donut + bars), and per-turn task summaries. |\n| Sidebar footer summary | Always-visible running count, total tokens, and cost. |\n| Right overview drawer | Collapsed by default; expands to a running-sessions + top-token-consumers + recent-activity panel with click-to-open. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Data source",
      "text": "| Displayed | Source |\n|---|---|\n| turns / steps / wall times | `sessionStats` projection |\n| input / output / cache tokens | `tokenUsage` projection |\n| context occupancy / composition | `contextPressure` + `contextBreakdown` projections |\n| per-day token history (heatmap) | `tokenHistory` projection (registered by this plugin) |\n| status | `SessionSummary.running` / `pendingInteraction` / `completed` |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Data source",
      "text": "Cost is estimated from DeepSeek's official pricing (V4-Flash / V4-Pro, cache-hit / cache-miss / output priced separately) with USD / CNY / EUR / GBP / JPY switching."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires the `dsh` CLI ([install DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)).\n\n```sh"
    },
    {
      "section": "from GitHub (recommended)",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add github:wellorbetter/dsh-plugin-window-stats"
    },
    {
      "section": "or from a local checkout",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-plugin-window-stats\n```\n\nRestart the profile (`dsh web`) after installing. The plugin is a [bundle](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/master/docs/user/develop/basic/publish.md): it declares `dsh.bundle.patch`, so `dsh plugin` reconciles it into the profile's `dsh.profile.bundles` automatically. It ships pre-built JavaScript (`lib/`), so a GitHub install needs no build step or `allowBuilds` permission."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "- **Sidebar** — the footer shows running count + total tokens + cost at all times.\n- **窗口统计 tab** — open any session and click the tab to see every session's progress, tokens, and cost; click a row for a rich breakdown; use the toolbar to sort / filter / group / switch model & currency.\n- **会话分析 tab** — analyze the current session over a time range, by tool type, with a token trend chart and task summaries.\n- **Right drawer** — click the edge handle to expand the running / top-tokens / recent overview, click any row to open it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\npnpm install\npnpm verify   # typecheck + build + test\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
